Default to native Wayland instead of preferring X11.

Upstream pins the GTK backend order to X11-first (XWayland) for its
F11 fullscreen key grab. That grab backend (global-hotkey on Linux)
is X11-only and stays inert without an X connection, so the pin
buys nothing on Wayland sessions while forcing everything through
XWayland. Drop the override so GTK takes the session default;
an explicit GDK_BACKEND keeps working, handled by GTK itself.
The desktop entry already carries the application ID, and its
StartupWMClass is aligned with it for correct Wayland grouping.

